      "content": "TL 00 SE            ABBOTS LANGLEY         SERGEHILL LANE                                            (Northwest side)                                            Bedmond 3/65                                       Church of the 9.5.78                                     Ascension II Parish church. Built in 1880 for £80 given by W.H. Solly. Pre-fabricated in corrugated iron, walls painted cream on a rendered brick plinth. Gothic Revival Style. W porch. 4 bay nave. SW tower and steeple. 1 bay chancel with vestry outshuts.  Gabled entrance porch: pointed arched entrance, cusped finialed bargeboards. W end 2 light Y traceried window with timber hood mould, wavy finialed bargeboards. Tower has a louvred trefoil headed lancet to W, splay footed octagonal belfry with trefoil headed louvred openings. Octagonal spire with elaborate iron finial. Nave has 4 lancet windows in chamfered timber surrounds to each side. Chancel  E  window  is  3  lights  with  intersecting  tracery,  wavy bargeboards. Lean-to to N with 2 light window to E and an entrance to W. Smaller lean-to to S with an entrance to E. Interior: completely wood panelled. Simple collar truss roof. Around pointed chancel arch and on wall plates are painted mottos. Listing NGR: TL0986803891"
    }
  ],
